NAME

ulibSetBit - Sets the value of a bit in a bit field


SYNOPSIS

void ulibSetBit(UBYTE *StartByte, long Position, long Value)
                       a0              d0            d1


DESCRIPTION

This function works in the same way as ulibBit(), except that it sets bit
number <Position> to <Value> (where <Value> is 0 or 1).

<StartByte> points to the beginning of an unbounded array, and bitfields run
in a rather strange manner (see the description of ulibBit() above).


NOTES

This function is used internally by Xenolink, and will not be useful to
application developers.  This function will most likely be discontinued in
version 2.0 of Xenolink.


